The  driver  provides support for a process to address devices on
the bus for which there is no configured driver.  A adapter  must
also  be separately configured into the system before this driver
makes sense.  If a is given, that number of devices will be  con‐
figured into the kernel.  The driver has no ioctls of its own but
rather  acts  as  a medium for the generic ioctls.  These are de‐
scribed in unknown devices.  All debug ioctls  work  on  devices.
